A||||1||Voyd||sunroof seal?||||1
Z||000000||Voyd||11-09-1999||03:21 AM||||today i went on a trip and it was the first  time i went on the highway for a long period of time with my Fiero. <P>at speeds of about 110km/h or more, there is a VERY loud wind sound coming from the sunroof, kinda like its letting massive amounts of air in, even louder than rolling down the window. The sunroof does not leak, to the best of my knowlledge. it rains alot here and ive never seen any wet spots or water anywhere in the car or on the headliner.<P>is it some kind of seal that isnt tight enough? cuz with this horrendous sound you almost have to yell to the person beside you.<P>thanks<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Carrolles||11-09-1999||07:44 AM||||Take a look at the sunroof gasket seal surface.  If it is leaking you will see a pattern in the dust/dirt on the seal.  Also you can insert a piece of paper like a 3x5 card between the glass and the gasket then close the roof.  Try to slide the paper around to see if it is loose at any part.<P>The rear latch mechanism can be tightened by adding another spacer between it and the roof structure (available from Pontiac dealer).  Also look at the hinge (the metal spades that are attached to the glass that stab into the holes at the front roof line) and see if the plastic coating is still on them.  The coating had peeled off of mine and caused the same problem you have.  I got new hinges and mounting bolts/seals from the  Pontiac dealer for about $12.00.  This really tightened up the glass to the gasket.<P>Clean off the gasket and wipe it down with some silicone spray.<P>Hope this helps,<BR>Carroll||||reg||1
